# Under Pressure Custom Apparel — Cloudflare Pages _redirects
# Place this file in customer-site/ (repo root for this Pages project)

# ── Root URL serves the store ────────────────────────────────────────
# The homepage file is named index.html, so Cloudflare Pages serves it
# at / natively — no rule needed here at all, which sidesteps the
# .html-stripping trap entirely (see note below). /store is just a
# friendly alias, rewritten straight to / (not to a filename), so it
# can't collide with the wildcard store rule either.
/store           /                             200

# ── Dynamic team stores ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: Do NOT add a /team-store rule targeting team-store.html (or any
# rule whose source path equals its own target's clean/extensionless
# form) — Cloudflare Pages automatically strips the .html extension off
# any served HTML file's canonical URL, so that combination creates an
# infinite redirect loop (ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS), not a working page.
# Team stores are already served at the clean path /team-store
# automatically. Every admin-created store still works at:
#   underpressurecustomapparel.com/team-store?team=<subdomain>

# ── Legacy named routes (kept for old links) ─────────────────────────
/rampage         /team-store?team=rampage          200
/rome            /team-store?team=rome             200

# ── Short store URLs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# underpressurecustomapparel.com/<subdomain> for any store, e.g.
# underpressurecustomapparel.com/thefamilystore. Rules above take
# precedence (first match wins), and any actual static file at that
# path (images, .b64 mockups, etc.) is always served before this is
# ever considered — Cloudflare only falls through to _redirects when
# no static asset matches the request path.
/:team           /team-store?team=:team            200
